<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Marley returns two weeks after digit-sparing en bloc excision of the nail unit of his right great toe, with a full-thickness skin graft from the inner upper arm and a right inguinal sentinel node biopsy, as a day case. The tie-over dressing came off at one week and the graft had taken. He took acetaminophen for nine days and needs nothing now. He walks in the stiff-soled postoperative shoe and has kept the foot raised when resting. The groin wound is comfortable, with no swelling. The final pathology is back. He has had no thoughts of self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Operation</td><td>Digit-sparing excision of the nail unit, full-thickness skin graft, and right inguinal sentinel node biopsy, as a day case</td></tr><tr><td>Pathology</td><td>No residual invasive melanoma; margins clear (closest 6 mm); both sentinel nodes negative</td></tr><tr><td>Final stage</td><td>pT1b pN0(sn) M0, pathologic stage IA</td></tr><tr><td>Recovery</td><td>Graft taken; walking in a postoperative shoe; no pain medicine</td></tr><tr><td>Plans</td><td>Wants to run and play football again, and to tour later in the year</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

